# Code owners.
#
# On the cluster, the boundary around production is RBAC: the `deployer` ServiceAccount has no
# rights there, and no path to that cluster at all. But production is *described* here, in files
# that the ISTAT DevOps team applies in good faith — and RBAC cannot see a pull request.
#
# So the separation of duties has to exist on both halves of the path. Below, the files that
# describe or reach production require a review from the team that operates it.
#
# Enforced only when branch protection has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled:
# see istat-ndc-cicd/docs/repo-governance.md.
#
# @istat/ndc-devops is a PLACEHOLDER, like the `istat-ndc-*` namespace root: the real team
# handle is to be agreed with ISTAT. Until it exists, GitHub ignores unknown owners silently,
# which is exactly why it must be one of the first things settled on day one.

*                               @ndc-dxc

# Applied to the cluster by INFRA/OPS: namespaces, quotas, RBAC, the deploy identity.
/bootstrap/                     @ndc-dxc @istat/ndc-devops

# The deploy identity's behaviour, including the guard that keeps the pipeline out of prod.
/tekton/tasks/helm-deploy.yaml  @ndc-dxc @istat/ndc-devops
